{"doc_id":"REPORT-news_r-05467-00001","summaries":{"A":{"adequacy":2,"critical_unsupported":1,"critical_omission":1,"wrong_unit_qualifier":0,"entity_relation":1,"fluency":2,"utility":2,"evidence":["바닥에 깔리는 박석은 강화 석모도와 해주에서 채석한 것만 사용하였는데","궁궐 공사 때 사용한 다양한 용도의 석재들은 서울 가까운 곳에서 얻었지만"],"reason":"The first sentence repeats itself, and the last sentence repeats the third. It says the stones were quarried nearby 'but' only Ganghwa and Haeju stones were used. That misstates the source, which says the nearby rule applied to stone in general and the paving stone was the exception. It also leaves out the rough finish's functions (glare reduction, anti-slip, drainage)."},"B":{"adequacy":2,"critical_unsupported":0,"critical_omission":1,"wrong_unit_qualifier":1,"entity_relation":0,"fluency":3,"utility":2,"evidence":["바닥에 깔리는 박석은 강화 석모도와 해주에서 채석한 것만 사용하였는데","1647년(인조 25) 창덕궁 공사 때 사용된 박석은 모두 강화도에서 채석되었고"],"reason":"It covers the quarry sources and the 1647 and 18th-century details. It omits the rough finish and its functions, which are the main point of the article. It also drops the scope that the Ganghwa and Haeju rule applied to paving stone, not all stone."},"C":{"adequacy":3,"critical_unsupported":0,"critical_omission":0,"wrong_unit_qualifier":0,"entity_relation":0,"fluency":3,"utility":4,"evidence":["박석의 거친 마감은 이런 자연현상에 대한 과학적인 배려로 빛의 되쏘임 현상을 차단하는 의도라고 볼 수 있다","1906년 경운궁 중건을 비롯해 대한제국 시절에 진행된 궁궐 공사에도 석모도에서 채석한 박석을 사용하였다"],"reason":"It keeps the rough finish and its glare-blocking purpose, the quarry sources, the 1647 and 1906 dates, and the harmony with nature. It leaves out anti-slip and drainage and is somewhat long-winded, but it has no clear errors."},"D":{"adequacy":1,"critical_unsupported":1,"critical_omission":1,"wrong_unit_qualifier":1,"entity_relation":1,"fluency":2,"utility":2,"evidence":["18세기 궁궐 공사 때는 창의문 밖이나 남산 아래 인근에서 채석했다고 한다","1906년 경운궁 중건을 비롯해 대한제국 시절에 진행된 궁궐 공사에도 석모도에서 채석한 박석을 사용하였다"],"reason":"It merges the quarry sources and eras wrongly. It says Ganghwa and Haeju stone was used in 1647, then that the 18th-century stone from outside Changuimun or below Namsan was also used in 1906. In the source the 18th-century stone came from a different place, and the 1906 stone came from Seokmo Island. It also omits the finish functions."}}}
